designs.metrics_and_statistics:
SUCCESS: VAL ('Plan valid' from bench/planbench/VAL validate.exe, run with the vendored Logistics domain through B.val_check(domain_path=…)) on the original instance PDDL. The exact executor (L.execute) gives a second score, and the disagreement count must be reported; it is expected to be 0. A scout reproduced all 1,450 published Logistics flags with the executor and VAL, 0 disagreements.

PRIMARY: exact two-sided McNemar of S-beam vs S-direct on the 40 identical IDs, using bwmn/stats.mcnemar_exact(b, c) (stats.py line 24), alpha 0.05. Reading as stated in question_and_claim.

ESTIMATES: success with Clopper-Pearson 95% CIs for both systems, overall and per package stratum (n = 10 each, descriptive). CP code exists in scripts/build_devfreeze.py line 34.

SECONDARY (descriptive, with no new claims beyond H1):
- success by optimal-length bin, using the published GT, which is optimal (Fast Downward astar(lmcut)): 13-19 (8), 20-29 (17), 30-41 (15);
- verification precision: the share of F-verified plans that VAL accepts (BP.score fields);
- failure modes (budget / dead_end / unparseable);
- plan length relative to optimal on solved instances;
- per-instance compute: proposer generated tokens, unique F queries, F tokens, wall s. FLOPs are estimated post hoc with bwmn/flops.py, the E-01(c) lesson;
- F-audit exact-match by package count, with CP CIs;
- the selection-set results for all configs, published in full;
- the val_oor vs test gap, descriptive only (val_oor is a selection set, so it is biased upward);
- paired exact McNemar against each of the 7 published per-instance files on the same 40 IDs, Holm-adjusted (bwmn/stats.holm, line 71), labelled 'different regime'.

MULTIPLICITY: there is one primary test, so no correction is needed. The Holm correction applies only to the published-comparator family.

POWER NOTE: n = 40 is chosen for GPU cost. It detects BW-like effects: B2 hard was 73/110 vs 5/110, and val_large K4 0.60 vs direct 0.117-0.133 (select.jsonl). At S-direct near 0, it needs S-beam at 6/40 or more.

ALLOWED CLAIMS:
- "Trained only on <=3-package generated Logistics problems, the same frozen 0.6B core with two LoRA adapters, planning without feedback, solves X/40 PlanBench Logistics instances with 4-7 packages (CI), vs Y/40 for the same proposer without the world model (McNemar p)."
- Not allowed: "beats o1-preview"; any statement about the reserved 245; obfuscated Logistics; any configuration chosen on test instances.
